nds out as the safest discard. It's an honor tile not matching any player\u2019s seat or prevalent wind (you are East, prevailing is South). No player has shown strong interest in F4 \u2014 only one discard from previous player, no pungs. It cannot form dangerous sequences like suited tiles.  \n- B4 and B5 are risky due to active play in B4-B6 range (next and previous players involved in chows around there).  \n- T8 and T6 are in suits where melds are active, especially T7 being konged, making T8 potentially useful for 7-8-9 chows.  \n- Thus, **F4** is least likely to assist opponents toward winning.\n\nAnswer: Play F4"}
